{"name":"Cement Greige","hex":"#b5aba4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cement","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A powdered substance produced by firing (calcining) calcium carbonate (limestone) and clay that develops strong cohesive properties when mixed with water. The main ingredient of concrete.","The paste-like substance resulting from mixing such a powder with water, or the rock-like substance that forms when it dries."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To affix with cement.","To overlay or coat with cement."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cement"},{"term":"greige","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of clothing, textiles, etc.: neither bleached nor dyed, nor otherwise fully processed; unfinished.","Of a colour like that of unbleached or undyed fabric, between grey and beige."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of unbleached or undyed fabric between grey and beige, closely akin to taupe.","Clothing, textiles, etc., which have neither been bleached nor dyed, nor otherwise fully processed; greige goods."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greige"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cement","blocks":[{"text":"A cement is a binder used for construction that sets, hardens, and adheres to other materials to bind them together. Cement is seldom used on its own, but rather to bind sand and gravel (aggregate) together. Cement mixed with fine aggregate produces mortar for masonry, or with sand and gravel, produces concrete. Concrete is the most widely used material in existence and is behind only water as the planet's most-consumed resource."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/USMC-110806-M-IX060-148.jpg/330px-USMC-110806-M-IX060-148.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cement","wikidata":"Q45190"},{"title":"Greige goods","blocks":[{"text":"Greige goods are loom state woven fabrics, or unprocessed knitted fabrics. Greige goods undergo many subsequent processes, for instance, dyeing, printing, bleaching, and finishing, prior to further converting to finished goods such as clothing, or other textile products. \"Grey fabrics\" is another term to refer to unfinished woven or knitted fabrics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Rolls_of_dressed_fibre._Silk_industry_%28spun_silk%29%2C_South_Manchester%2C_Conn.%2C_U.S.A_%28NYPL_b11707678-G90F070_013F%29.tiff/lossy-page1-330px-Rolls_of_dressed_fibre._Silk_industry_%28spun_silk%29%2C_South_Manchester%2C_Conn.%2C_U.S.A_%28NYPL_b11707678-G90F070_013F%29.tiff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greige_goods","wikidata":"Q105985607"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/LDClinkerScaled.jpg/500px-LDClinkerScaled.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/LDClinkerScaled.jpg/500px-LDClinkerScaled.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Clinker nodules produced by sintering at 1450 °C","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALDClinkerScaled.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Calcium_oxide_powder.JPG/500px-Calcium_oxide_powder.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Calcium_oxide_powder.JPG/1280px-Calcium_oxide_powder.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Calcium_oxide_powder.JPG/500px-Calcium_oxide_powder.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Calcium oxide obtained by thermal decomposition of calcium carbonate at high temperature (above 8